---
description: Frontend commit/PR title/body writing rules
globs: frontend/**/*, report/**/*
alwaysApply: true
---

- **Purpose**
  - Keep commit and PR messages consistent across the team.

- **Basic principle**
  - Frontend scope code is always `[{{SCOPE_CODE}}]`.
  - Context prefix uses the product code: `[{{PRODUCT_CODE}}]`.
  - Default prefix: `[{{PRODUCT_CODE}}][{{SCOPE_CODE}}]`

- **Commit message format**
  - `[{{PRODUCT_CODE}}][{{SCOPE_CODE}}]<emoji><type>: <subject> [#work-item]`
  - `emoji` and `type` must be written together without a space.
  - Strictly use 1:1 type/emoji mapping (no mixing).
  - `subject` should be concise, current-tense, factual. No trailing period.
  - No exaggerated or vague expressions — describe what actually changed.

- **Type/emoji mapping**
  - `✨feat`: new user-facing feature
  - `🐛fix`: bug fix
  - `♻️refactor`: behavior-preserving structural improvement
  - `💄feat`: UI/style improvement
  - `🌐update`: i18n resource change
  - `📦update`: frontend dependency update
  - `✅test`: add or update tests
  - `📝docs`: documentation change
  - `🔧chore`: build/config/tooling change
  - `🔥remove`: code or file removal

- **Type selection criteria**
  - `feat`: a user-visible behavior or feature is added
  - `fix`: a previously working behavior is broken and fixed
  - `refactor`: external behavior unchanged, internal structure improved
  - `update`: library or i18n resource updated
  - `chore`: non-product config or infrastructure change

- **PR title format**
  - `[{{PRODUCT_CODE}}][{{SCOPE_CODE}}]<emoji><type>: <summary> [#work-item]`
  - Omit `[#work-item]` if no work item is associated.

- **PR body template**
  - Use the template below as the default.
  - For complex changes, add `Background`, `Root Cause`, `Fix Approach`, `Test Details`, `Risk/Rollback Plan` sections as needed.

```markdown
## Summary
<!--- Describe why this change is needed and what problem it solves. -->
- Description
    - NA
- Intent
    - NA
- Effects
    - NA

## Related Work Item
<!--- Link the work item here -->

## PR Checklist
- [ ] I have reviewed my own code.
- [ ] I have added comments where the logic is not obvious.
- [ ] I have added or updated tests that prove this fix/feature works.

## Screenshots (if applicable)
```

- **Examples**
  - Commit
    - `[{{PRODUCT_CODE}}][{{SCOPE_CODE}}]🐛fix: fix patient info panel alignment [#65725]`
    - `[{{PRODUCT_CODE}}][{{SCOPE_CODE}}]💄feat: improve right panel typography readability`
    - `[{{PRODUCT_CODE}}][{{SCOPE_CODE}}]📦update: update react-query version`
  - PR title
    - `[{{PRODUCT_CODE}}][{{SCOPE_CODE}}]🐛fix: Figma update — fix result panel Patient Info text overflow and alignment [#65725]`
